    <owner-decision-required>
      🔔 PRODUCT/DESIGN DECISION (root §6.5 / §11) — the owner MUST choose before this task executes:
      Born-in-editor documents can contain native OOXML tables today (live `insertTable` toolbar command,
      mode-agnostic; `ComposeContentModel.Table` + `ComposeDocumentRenderer.SynthesizeDocument` author real
      `w:tbl`), but the task-003 operation schema is a CLOSED 10-op union with NO table-authoring primitive, and
      `ComposeShadowPatchEngine` only refuses-across tables (never authors them). So born-in-editor-with-a-table
      cannot be saved under the unified op model. Choose:
      • Path B — EXTEND the op schema (FR-11 spine) with a table-authoring family (`insertTable`/`insertTableRow`/
        `insertTableCell`, or a coarser `insertBlock` carrying an embedded content sub-model), teach the engine to
        author `w:tbl` onto an empty shadow package, then unify born-in-editor (FR-09) fully + retire
        `ComposeDocumentRenderer`/`buildContentModel`. Preserves the shipped capability; completes I-5 one-byte-author.
      • Path C — REMOVE table authoring from the born-in-editor surface (disable `insertTable` when there is no
        loaded baseline); tables become import-only. Lets FR-09 "no separate full-render path" hold literally.
        A product-visible feature regression — needs explicit owner sign-off.
      Until chosen, born-in-editor stays on the `ComposeDocumentRenderer` path (working, no regression) — a
      documented §6.5 Path-A interim exception (a scoped second byte-author).
    </owner-decision-required>
  </metadata>

